A||||25||Mark Matthews||New to Board & Fieros||||3||
Z||000000||Mark Matthews||11-29-2001||11:27 AM||||Hi all, great looking/busy board you got going here.  I've been looking into the Fieros just recently and would like to hear from you guys about them.  The reason I got interested in them was from the cool kitcars you can make from them.  How does everybody feel about these?<P>I've seen some stuff on the net about that they have pretty good crash ratings, but they have some heat trouble due to the mid-engine.  Opinions?<P>I know the fiero is for the street, but the kit the really interested me was the Jalapeno by PISA.  Anyone tried this, how's it work, who hates it?  I love the 4x4 look however I don't plan to do any 4x4ing.  I have an old FJ40 that I've done my share with.<P>I'm in Vegas, any other Vegas Fieros crew out here?  I'd like to go with the V6 for the conversion, if I do it.  Anything else to look for, or keep an eye out for?<P>Thanks for you time!<P>------------------<BR>Mark Matthews<BR>'70 BMW 2002<BR>'57 Chevy BelAir||||reg||3
Z||000001||ITB 2M4||11-29-2001||11:49 AM||||Welcome to the board!  Seems like you've got a couple of interesting non-fieros to drive around in as well.<P>The cooling is more of a problem on the 4 cyl., as it only came with 3.5 qts. of oil from the factory.  They tend to leak as they get older, and 2.5 qts. (or less) of oil in a mid-engine car doesn't do any good.  I'm racing a 4 cyl. car, and have an Accusump 3 qt. oil tank, an oil cooler, and a remote filter, for a grand total of 10 qts. oil.  The car runs at 200 degrees or less in the Florida heat while running hard.<P>Not real familiar with the Jalepeno kit,  but I know PISA has been around a while.  There is a really nice GT-40 kit out there as well, but to do it right, you need the stretch kit, otherwise it looks to short.  That, along with a ZZ4 crate motor from GM, and a Porsche transaxle would be a sweet combination.<P>Again, welcome to the board, and have fun.<P>------------------<BR>SCCA ITB '84 Fiero 2M4||||reg||10
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||11-29-2001||12:06 PM||||Welcome to the forum!  I really quite like the look/functionality of the Jalapeno (especially for winters here in Minnesota).  Maybe in the near future.<P>I too have always been very interested in the KitCar scene with the Fiero. I nearly purchased an F355 kit in South Carolina last year.  But what I learned quickly is that the kit car industry can be a shady one (at least there are a few recurring shady scam artists out there).  But if you take the time and money you can achieve an amazing final product.<P>As to the heat issues... as stated above heat isn't necessarily the true issue. It's the oiling system inherint in the engines used.  They didn't solve this issue until the '88 model year.  Dealing with a car that is 15 years old has it's own normal wear-and-tear issues (as I'm sure you're aware driving older vehicles).  Engine swaps have become commonplace with the 3.1/3.4 V6 being one of the easiest and most common (basically a drop in solution).<P>Ask whatever questions you can think of, and use the search function at the top of the page to dig for past posts relating to common questions.<P>Again- Welcome!  Be warned, Fieros are very addictive.<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||84Bill||11-29-2001||12:16 PM||||Hi & Welcome<P>The Jalapeno is a very cool off road kit for the Fiero and looks great in person. I saw one at Carlisle this past spring. Skitime has some pictures of it and if he happens to pass through I'm sure he will post a few for you.<BR>||||reg||7
Z||000004||Mark Matthews||11-29-2001||12:41 PM||||Thanks for the replys guys, wow, this board is as busy as the one for my 2002, if not more busy.<P>Yeah, I really love the look of the Jalapeno, plus for a first kitcar, it sounds like it's easy to do.  The one thing that I'm not too sure about is the whole fibarglass thing.  I've never done fibarglass work, and I guess I should ask PISA this, but are most of the kits bolt on (using existing holes), or like rivet, etc.<P>Yeah, my like '02 is very fun to drive, but I'm really in to the custom stuff and there are too many options, with out paying up the wazzue.  I don't mess with '57 too much, it's original.<P>Well, thanks again for the replys, I'd love to see those pictures if he pops in.<P>edit :: Also, if I were to do the 3" suspension lift with 30" tires, hows the rear diff gonna hold up?  Are they LSD?<p>[This message has been edited by Mark Matthews (edited 11-29-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000005||BAM-BAM||11-29-2001||12:50 PM||||Mark, hey I am from Vegas! I have been on the board here quite a while. You will find that this is about the best place in the world to get information on or about anything to do with Fiero's. As for the PISA Jalapeno, you will find some mixed feeling here about PISA in general. Have never seen a Jalapeno in the real. Your name sound familiar to me in regards to Fiero's, you sure you haven't owned one before???<BR>Anyway, hit me back via E-Mail and maybe we can get together. bartlettds@lvcm.com <P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000006||MinnGreenGT||11-29-2001||01:08 PM||||Mark... the Fiero actually does not have an LSD.  Athough there was some discussion here (within the last month or two) about an aftermarket one becoming available at a reasonable cost. <BR>( <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/014792.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/014792.html</A>  )<P>As to your question about working with Fiberglass... PISA Corp has been around longer than most companies, and appears to be a stable corperation. But they are also know for "stealing" ideas from other people/companies and claiming them as their own.  I'd deal with them based on their reliablility, but if someone else (the creator of a product) sells it elsewhere- I'd rather go there.  The Jalapeno design is an original to PISA btw.<P>Have you checked out their website at <A HREF="http://www.cybercars.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cybercars.com</A>  ? Click on PISA/Fiero H.Q.<p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 11-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Joe Torma||11-29-2001||01:39 PM||||Jalepeno...eeewwww.<BR>Fiero=go fast not go muddin'.<P>Just my opinion.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Welcome!!!||||reg||1
